00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.960
Prospective new partner, if he likes us.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.040
Liking ain't the problem. Trusting is, as I said.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:30.880
Keep your voices down. I don't want my boss hearing.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:32.580
This is a sideline.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:35.380
Of course. Look at us. Honest as the day is long.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:36.000
Exactly.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:38.540
I tell you what. Let us prove ourselves.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.380
Prove ourselves? To this clown? What you talking about?

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:45.060
Good day, Hosea. Good luck with your business dealings.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:48.040
Listen, he's rough and ready and quick with his tongue,

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.140
but I swear you can trust him and trust me.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:51.580
I'm an old man.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:53.100
You're not old, Seamus.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.900
I'm old enough. And you know why I ain't dead?

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:57.020
You don't trust idiots.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:57.820
Exactly.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:01.040
We're not idiots. Let us prove it to you.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:05.540
Okay. I'll tell you what.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:06.300
Arthur!

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:11.300
Old Bob Crawford and his boys just bought a beautiful stolen stagecoach from Upstate.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:12.540
It's in their barn.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:13.960
Now you go get that.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:16.960
And then we can work together.

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:18.660
Who's old Bob Crawford?

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:19.800
An acquaintance of mine.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.000
So you want us to take out your competition?

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:25.420
Well, he's not just an acquaintance, but a cousin.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:26.800
By marriage.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.000
